","fullName":"Sen. Hawley, Josh [R-MO]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-08","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MO"},{"bioguideId":"G000386","fullName":"Sen. Grassley, Chuck [R-IA]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-09-30","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IA"},{"bioguideId":"M000355","fullName":"Sen. McConnell, Mitch [R-KY]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-10-23","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"KY"},{"bioguideId":"G000608","fullName":"Sen. Graham, Darline [R-SC]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-07-27","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"SC"},{"bioguideId":"Y000064","fullName":"Sen. Young, Todd [R-IN]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-09-16","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IN"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-17T14:50:11+00:00","id":"s401-119","introducedDate":"2025-02-04","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-02-04","text":"Read twice and referred to the Committee on Banking, Housing, and Urban Affairs."},"laws":[],"number":"401","originChamber":"Senate","policyArea":"Finance and Financial Sector","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"C001096","district":null,"fullName":"Sen. Cramer, Kevin [R-ND]","party":"R","state":"ND"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-02-04","actionDesc":"Introduced in Senate","text":"<p><strong>Fair Access to Banking Act </strong></p><p>This bill places restrictions on certain banks, credit unions, and payment card networks if they refuse to do business with a person who complies with the law. Restrictions include prohibiting the use of electronic funds transfer systems and lending programs, termination of an institution's depository insurance, and specified civil penalties.</p><p>Banks and other specified financial institutions are allowed to deny financial services to a person only if the denial is justified by a documented failure of that person to meet quantitative, impartial, risk-based standards established in advance by the institution. This justification may not be based upon reputational risks to the institution.</p><p>The bill establishes the right for a person to bring a civil action for a violation of this bill.</p>","updateDate":"2025-07-21T20:26:46Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Fair Access to Banking Act","type":"s","updateDate":"2026-09-17T11:03:28Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-17T11:03:28Z"}
